' Key names — Roku's onKeyEvent already delivers clean lowercase names (plus "OK"/"back").
' Centralized here so screens compare against Keys.* instead of magic strings — the seed of the
' input layer manager (full LAYER/mode/semaphore stack lands in Phase 6/9 when overlapping layers
' — guide/player/surf/modal — actually exercise it; see .plans/roku.md Phase 1).
'
' NOTE: standard Roku remotes have NO number pad and NO channel +/- keys, unlike LG/Apple remotes.
' Number entry + CH+/- (tv-web/tv-native features) may map to on-screen affordances instead — decide
' in Phase 9. The media keys below exist on most Roku remotes (rewind/ff/replay/play/options).
namespace Keys
    const UP = "up"
    const DOWN = "down"
    const LEFT = "left"
    const RIGHT = "right"
    const OK = "OK"
    const BACK = "back"
    const PLAY = "play"
    const REWIND = "rewind"
    const FORWARD = "fastforward"
    const REPLAY = "replay"
    const OPTIONS = "options"
end namespace
